Feature: Flight modes
  One press selects the next flight mode: MANUAL, then [[ANGLE]], then [[ACRO]], then MANUAL
  again. On a keyboard, press M. On a radio, press the button you gave to ArduPilot mode. The
  top line of the HUD shows the mode.

  The T1-S VTOL flies with ArduPilot, and its radio has six modes on six buttons: QHOVER, QLOITER,
  FBWA, CRUISE, AUTO and QRTL. FBWA is its self-levelling mode, like ANGLE. [[The six buttons of
  the radio]] says what each one does. Two tutorials fly the VTOL with them: [[Flying a VTOL with
  self-levelling]] takes off, flies forward in FBWA, and lands softly, and [[Trying the buttons of
  the radio]] tries the other modes.

  Expectation: ANGLE levels the plane for you
    In ANGLE, the sticks set the angle of bank and pitch. When you release the sticks, the
    plane levels its wings and nose. Use this mode when you learn to fly.
    Given the flight controller is fitted
    And the flight mode is MANUAL
    When the pilot changes flight mode
    Then the flight mode is ANGLE

  Expectation: In ANGLE, the stick sets the bank
    Hold A or D, and the plane banks to an angle of 55° or less. It does not roll over.
    Given the flight mode is ANGLE
    And the plane is flying
    When the pilot rolls the plane to the left
    Then the wings are banked

  Expectation: In ANGLE, the wings become level again
    Release the stick, and the plane levels its wings by itself.
    Given the flight mode is ANGLE
    And the plane is flying
    And the wings are banked
    When the pilot releases the roll stick
    Then the wings are level

  Expectation: ACRO holds the attitude
    In ACRO, the sticks set the rate of roll and pitch. When you centre the sticks, the plane
    holds its attitude, also when it is upside down. Use this mode for aerobatics.
    Given the flight controller is fitted
    And the flight mode is ANGLE
    When the pilot changes flight mode
    Then the flight mode is ACRO

  Expectation: MANUAL gives you the control surfaces
    In MANUAL, the sticks move the ailerons, the elevator and the rudder directly. Nothing
    helps you. The plane flies as the real plane does.
    Given the flight controller is fitted
    And the flight mode is ACRO
    When the pilot changes flight mode
    Then the flight mode is MANUAL
